{"id":"workloads-controllers-job","corpus":"k8s","title":"Jobs","sourceUrl":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/workloads/controllers/job/","license":"Kubernetes Documentation © The Kubernetes Authors, licensed CC BY 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","blocks":[{"kind":"h1","text":"Jobs"},{"kind":"p","text":"Jobs represent one-off tasks that run to completion and then stop."},{"kind":"p","text":"A Job creates one or more Pods and will continue to retry execution of the Pods until a specified number of them successfully terminate. As pods successfully complete, the Job tracks the successful completions. When a specified number of successful completions is reached, the task (ie, Job) is complete. Deleting a Job will clean up the Pods it created. Suspending a Job will delete its active Pods until the Job is resumed again."},{"kind":"p","text":"A simple case is to create one Job object in order to reliably run one Pod to completion. The Job object will start a new Pod if the first Pod fails or is deleted (for example due to a node hardware failure or a node reboot)."},{"kind":"p","text":"You can also use a Job to run multiple Pods in parallel."},{"kind":"p","text":"If you want to run a Job (either a single task, or several in parallel) on a schedule, see CronJob."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Running an example Job"},{"kind":"p","text":"Here is an example Job config. It computes π to 2000 places and prints it out. It takes around 10s to complete."},{"kind":"p","text":"You can run the example with this command:"},{"kind":"p","text":"The output is similar to this:"},{"kind":"p","text":"Check on the status of the Job with kubectl:"},{"kind":"p","text":"To view completed Pods of a Job, use kubectl get pods."},{"kind":"p","text":"To list all the Pods that belong to a Job in a machine readable form, you can use a command like this:"},{"kind":"p","text":"The output is similar to this:"},{"kind":"p","text":"Here, the selector is the same as the selector for the Job. The --output=jsonpath option specifies an expression with the name from each Pod in the returned list."},{"kind":"p","text":"View the standard output of one of the pods:"},{"kind":"p","text":"Another way to view the logs of a Job:"},{"kind":"p","text":"The output is similar to this:"},{"kind":"h2","text":"Writing a Job spec"},{"kind":"p","text":"As with all other Kubernetes config, a Job needs apiVersion, kind, and metadata fields."},{"kind":"p","text":"When the control plane creates new Pods for a Job, the .metadata.name of the Job is part of the basis for naming those Pods. The name of a Job must be a valid DNS subdomain value, but this can produce unexpected results for the Pod hostnames. For best compatibility, the name should follow the more restrictive rules for a DNS label. Even when the name is a DNS subdomain, the name must be no longer than 63 characters."},{"kind":"p","text":"A Job also needs a .spec section."},{"kind":"h3","text":"Job Labels"},{"kind":"p","text":"Job labels will have batch.kubernetes.io/ prefix for job-name and controller-uid."},{"kind":"h3","text":"Pod Template"},{"kind":"p","text":"The .spec.template is the only required field of the .spec."},{"kind":"p","text":"The .spec.template is a pod template. It has exactly the same schema as a Pod, except it is nested and does not have an apiVersion or kind."},{"kind":"p","text":"In addition to required fields for a Pod, a pod template in a Job must specify appropriate labels (see pod selector) and an appropriate restart policy."},{"kind":"p","text":"Only a RestartPolicy equal to Never or OnFailure is allowed."},{"kind":"h3","text":"Pod selector"},{"kind":"p","text":"The .spec.selector field is optional. In almost all cases you should not specify it. See section specifying your own pod selector."},{"kind":"h3","text":"Parallel execution for Jobs"},{"kind":"p","text":"There are three main types of task suitable to run as a Job:"},{"kind":"li","text":"Non-parallel Jobs"},{"kind":"li","text":"normally, only one Pod is started, unless the Pod fails."},{"kind":"li","text":"the Job is complete as soon as its Pod terminates successfully."},{"kind":"li","text":"Parallel Jobs with a fixed completion count:"},{"kind":"li","text":"specify a non-zero positive value for .spec.completions."},{"kind":"li","text":"the Job represents the overall task, and is complete when there are .spec.completions successful Pods."},{"kind":"li","text":"when using .spec.completionMode=\"Indexed\", each Pod gets a different index in the range 0 to .spec.completions-1."},{"kind":"li","text":"Parallel Jobs with a work queue:"},{"kind":"li","text":"do not specify .spec.completions, default to .spec.parallelism."},{"kind":"li","text":"the Pods must coordinate amongst themselves or an external service to determine what each should work on. For example, a Pod might fetch a batch of up to N items from the work queue."},{"kind":"li","text":"each Pod is independently capable of determining whether or not all its peers are done, and thus that the entire Job is done."},{"kind":"li","text":"when any Pod from the Job terminates with success, no new Pods are created."}],"lemmas":{"jobs":["job","jobs"],"represented":["represented","represent"],"representing":["representing","represent"],"ones":["one","ones"],"offs":["offs","off"],"offing":["offing","off"],"tasks":["task","tasks"],"runs":["run","runs"],"ran":["ran","run"],"stops":["stop","stops"],"stopped":["stopped","stop"],"stopping":["stopping","stop"],"creates":["creates","create"],"creating":["creating","create"],"pods":["pod","pods"],"wills":["will","wills"],"willing":["willing","will"],"willed":["willed","will"],"would":["would","will"],"continues":["continues","continue"],"continued":["continued","continue"],"continuing":["continuing","continue"],"retries":["retries","retry"],"executions":["execution","executions"],"untils":["untils","until"],"specified":["specified","specify"],"specifieds":["specifieds","specified"],"numbers":["num